\DOC XMM_EXISTSTOP_TAC

\TYPE {XMM_EXISTSTOP_TAC : string -> term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Replaces an assumption giving the value of the lower half of a vector register
by an assumption giving the value of the whole register as that value joined
with a freshly named variable for the upper half.

\DESCRIBE
{top : string} names the new free variable standing for the upper half, and
{y : term} is the full-width register component whose read assumption is
introduced. The tactic deletes from the assumptions the equation that reads the
narrow (lower-half) component of the register in the current state and equates
it to some term {u}, and appends a new equation reading the component named by
{y} in that same state, equating it to the join of a new variable named by
{top} with {u}. The conclusion and all other assumptions are unchanged.
{
   A, (narrow read of register in state = u) ?- t
   =========================================  XMM_EXISTSTOP_TAC top y
   A, (read of y in state = join top u) ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces only this one kind of transformation occurs, always on a
goal whose conclusion is an {eventually} statement about a state that already
carries such a narrow-register read assumption.

\ENDDOC
